# OpenCode Custom Provider Configuration (OpenAI-Compatible)

## Configuration Overview

OpenCode supports custom OpenAI-compatible providers by configuring them in an `opencode.json` (or `opencode.jsonc`) file. Here's a complete setup guide based on the latest 2025 documentation:

## Config File Location

| Location | Purpose |
|----------|---------|
| `~/.config/opencode/opencode.json` | **Global config** — themes, providers, keybinds |
| `./opencode.json` (project root) | **Per-project config** — takes precedence over global |
| `OPENCODE_CONFIG` env var | **Custom path** — highest precedence |

OpenCode supports both `.json` and `.jsonc` (JSON with Comments) formats.

## Schema & Config Template

```jsonc
{
  "$schema": "https://opencode.ai/config.json",
  "model": "my-provider/model-id",
  "provider": {
    "my-provider": {
      "npm": "@ai-sdk/openai-compatible",
      "name": "My Custom Provider",
      "options": {
        "baseURL": "https://api.example.com/v1"
        // "apiKey": "sk-..." // optional if using auth.json instead
        // "headers": { "Authorization": "Bearer your-token" } // optional
      },
      "models": {
        "model-id": {
          "name": "Display Name"
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
```

## Authentication Setup (Two Options)

### Option 1: API Key in Config
```jsonc
"options": {
  "baseURL": "https://api.example.com/v1",
  "apiKey": "sk-your-key-here"
}
```

### Option 2: Separate Auth File
Run `opencode auth login` → select **Other** → enter a provider ID and API key. Keys are stored in `~/.local/share/opencode/auth.json`:
```json
{
  "my-provider": {
    "type": "api",
    "key": "sk-..."
  }
}
```

## Real-World Examples

**LM Studio (local):**
```jsonc
"lmstudio": {
  "npm": "@ai-sdk/openai-compatible",
  "name": "LM Studio (local)",
  "options": {
    "baseURL": "http://127.0.0.1:1234/v1"
  },
  "models": {
    "qwen/qwen3-coder-30b": { "name": "Qwen 3 Coder 30B" }
  }
}
```

**Ollama (local):**
```jsonc
"ollama": {
  "npm": "@ai-sdk/openai-compatible",
  "options": {
    "baseURL": "http://localhost:11434/v1"
  },
  "models": {
    "qwen2.5-coder": {}
  }
}
```

**Cerebras:**
```jsonc
"cerebras": {
  "npm": "@ai-sdk/openai-compatible",
  "name": "Cerebras",
  "options": {
    "baseURL": "https://api.cerebras.ai/v1",
    "apiKey": "csk-..."
  },
  "models": {
    "llama-3.3-70b": { "name": "Llama-3.3-70b" }
  }
}
```

**Azure OpenAI:**
```jsonc
"azure": {
  "options": {
    "baseURL": "https://{resource}.openai.azure.com",
    "resourceName": "my-resource"
  },
  "models": {
    "gpt-4.1-mini": { "name": "GPT-4.1 Mini" }
  }
}
```

## Key Configuration Fields

| Field | Description |
|-------|-------------|
| `npm` | Must be `"@ai-sdk/openai-compatible"` for OpenAI-compatible endpoints |
| `options.baseURL` | API endpoint URL (include `/v1` path) |
| `options.apiKey` | API key (optional if using auth.json) |
| `options.headers` | Custom headers (e.g., `"Authorization": "Bearer ..."`) |
| `models` | Map of model IDs to display names; model key should NOT include the provider prefix |

## Known Issues (2025)

1. **Empty options bug** (#5674): In some OpenCode versions, `baseURL` and `apiKey` from `options` are not being passed to API calls when using the bundled `@ai-sdk/openai-compatible` provider. The `options` object appears empty in debug logs, resulting in `NotFoundError`.

2. **Provider ID in model key**: Don't prefix the model key with the provider ID (e.g., use `"gpt-4.1-mini"` not `"azure/gpt-4.1-mini"`).

3. **Custom providers not in `/provider` command** (#5250): Custom providers configured in `opencode.jsonc` don't appear in the `/provider` command listing.

4. **Auth loop issue** (#976): After using the "Other" flow to save credentials, OpenCode may loop back to the provider selection screen — configuring `apiKey` directly in `options` can work around this.

5. **Auto-discovery request** (#6231): There's an active feature request for OpenCode to auto-discover available models from the `/v1/models` endpoint rather than requiring manual model listing.

## Documentation Links

- **Official Config docs**: `https://thdxr.dev.opencode.ai/docs/config/` (or `https://opencode.ai/docs/config/`)
- **Official Providers docs**: `https://thdxr.dev.opencode.ai/docs/providers/`


